# WishWorld build switches. Copy to .env and edit; .env is not committed.
# Only keys starting with WISHWORLD_ are copied into the app (see Assets/WishWorld/Editor/EnvSync.cs).

# Controller input on the headset.
#   ovr     Meta's OVRInput (default). Falls back to openxr by itself if it sees no controller.
#   openxr  Unity's XR input devices through OpenXR (the original path).
WISHWORLD_INPUT=ovr

# Creature and prop models used by WishWorld > Rebuild All.
#   packs      free CC0 packs where one exists, own builds otherwise (default)
#   generated  only models generated by this project (no third-party assets)
WISHWORLD_MODELS=packs

# What surrounds the Snow Circuit race track.
#   world  an alpine valley with mountains, forest, a village and trackside buildings (default)
#   room   the real room through passthrough, with only the track and car drawn (the original plan)
WISHWORLD_RACE_VIEW=world

# How many computer-driven cars race against you in Snow Circuit (0 to 5). 0 brings back the ghost car alone.
WISHWORLD_RACE_RIVALS=4

# The guide says the name of a button or card when it is pointed at for half a second (for children who cannot read yet).
#   on (default) or off
WISHWORLD_READ_BUTTONS=on

# Only when playing from a Windows PC through Meta Horizon Link: show the real room in Frost Slice and AR mode.
# Needs passthrough over Link switched on in the Link app. off (default) uses a grey backdrop.
WISHWORLD_LINK_PASSTHROUGH=off

# Gifts from the WishWorld web app (a family member's phone). With a web address here, the game asks that site
# every 2.5 seconds for new gifts in the room below; each creature gift appears in the world on show and the guide
# reads out its message. Leave the address empty (or the line commented out) and the game never contacts the site.
# The address is not a secret; it is copied into the app with the other WISHWORLD_ keys.
#   WISHWORLD_WEB_URL  the site's address, with no trailing slash, for example https://wishworld-web.netlify.app
#   WISHWORLD_ROOM     the room code shown on the web app's first page: 3 to 8 letters or digits (default WISH)
# WISHWORLD_WEB_URL=https://wishworld-web.netlify.app
WISHWORLD_ROOM=WISH

# "Scan a toy": a staged scan that ends with a toy the team modelled ahead of time joining the world (Bubby).
# Nothing is captured by the headset. See Assets/WishWorld/Editor/Builder.Toy.cs and Scripts/Worlds/ToyScan.cs.
#   on   the toy is built by WishWorld > Rebuild All and "scan a toy" is in the menu and the commands (default)
#   off  no toy and no scan. Takes effect at once; run WishWorld > Rebuild All to also remove the toy's files.
WISHWORLD_TOY=on

# The child's name, when it is known before the session. The toy greets the child by it ("Hi Sam! ...") without
# asking. Left empty, the guide asks "What's your name?" after the scan and uses the next thing said (hold A and
# speak); with no answer the toy says "friend". Set it for a planned demo, then run WishWorld > Voice > Bake Preset
# Lines so the greeting plays from the recording with no network.
# Like every WISHWORLD_ key this is copied into the app, so a name set here is inside any APK built with it.
# WISHWORLD_CHILD_NAME=

# --- Service keys. These are NOT copied into WishWorldEnv.txt. They go into the service config asset
# --- (Assets/WishWorld/Config/Resources/WishWorldServiceConfig.asset, not in version control) and switch the
# --- matching services on. That asset is part of the app, so a key placed here ships inside the APK:
# --- use keys you can revoke, and remove them before sharing a build.
#
# ElevenLabs: the guide's voice and push-to-talk speech recognition.
#   With the key and a voice id set, run WishWorld > Voice > Bake Preset Lines once: every preset line
#   (greetings, creature facts, quiz questions) is recorded into the app, so those play with no network.
#   WishWorld > Voice > List My ElevenLabs Voices prints the voice ids on your account.
#   With a key and no voice id, the stock voice "Jessica" is used.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=
#   Optional: a second account side by side. ELEVENLABS_ACCOUNT=2 makes the app use ELEVENLABS_API_KEY2.
# ELEVENLABS_ACCOUNT=1
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY2=
#   Optional: the model that records the preset lines. eleven_flash_v2_5 costs half as much as eleven_multilingual_v2.
# ELEVENLABS_BAKE_MODEL=eleven_flash_v2_5
#
# Claude (Anthropic): after speech recognition, picks the preset choices that come closest to a spoken wish, and lets
# the guide answer a child's question. Used instead of Gemini when present.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
#
# Gemini: the same job, used only when there is no Claude key.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
